outcomeRecord: "---\nslug: fix-instruction-conflicts\nshipped: 2026-10-18\nschemaVersion: 1\ndraft: true\n---\n# fix-instruction-conflicts\n\nDraft only: content judgment is still required.\nRead the collected evidence before choosing durable destinations.\nNo upgrade or coverage decision has been applied.\n\n- outcome: needs-decision\n- docs: none\n- decisions: none\n- knowledge: none\n- code: none\n- verification: none\n- followups: none\n- archive: none\n"
evidence[1]{path,hash,excerpt,truncated}:
  ".project/done-work.md#fix-instruction-conflicts","sha256:797ce194894dbd26d1ca8bbb2a6074494da5f41d1fe70da175a789500e3f93ed","## fix-instruction-conflicts — shipped 2026-10-18\n\nA bug-fix pass (2.31.1–2.31.4, 2026-10-17 to 2026-10-18) made conflicting workflow instructions agree, each topic with one authoritative owner, without removing any gate, reviewer, evidence requirement or permission boundary. Triage came from an owner-supplied static analysis; every finding was verified against the checkout before any edit. Findings and their owners: A Orca exit 3 was \"continue normally\" in the audit and ship phase specs but \"stop and ask\" in the skills and in `orca-run.mts` `exitCodeFor`, so with Orca requested a refused dispatch could silently fall back; `orca-vendors.md` now owns the decision (\"exit code 3 alone never authorizes the normal path\", with the off, bypassed, worker, ready and stop outcomes, and exit 4 documented). B/C the security reviewer had Write/Edit and was told to remediate while its OpenCode and Codex adapters were read-only, and a clean review was told to print only \"No security findings\"; the canonical prompt is now `Read, Bash, Grep, Glob`, inspect and report only, proofs of concept only in a scratch copy, one summary for every review with Checked and Unverified and a `PASS | BLOCK | INCOMPLETE` verdict (unfinished is never PASS). D three size limits (800 lines in the code reviewer, a hard 150 default in `component-architecture.md`, a soft signal in `coding-standards.md`); `component-architecture.md` is the single owner (project limit, else 150/80/50, the cohesive-unit exception the only way past). E the build gate disagreed between the skill, `2-build.md` and the overview matrix, which had no `/build end` row; the matrix owns it now with the union (auto / gated / gated / gated) and the skill and spec defer to it. F mirrors were documented as pointers only although Cursor holds byte copies; `docs/vendors.md` documents both mechanisms and the refresh procedure (`cursor-mirrors` lists `differs`; copy the canonical file). G entry files and modes: an existing `@AGENTS.md` import",true
